WEBVTT

00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:17.130
Nusumareta kako wo

00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:20.330
Sagashitsuzukete

00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:23.420
Ore wa samayou

00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:27.130
Mishiranu machi wo

00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:32.080
Honou no nioi shimitsuite

00:00:32.330 --> 00:00:33.880
Museru

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:37.630
Sayonara wa itta hazu da

00:00:37.630 --> 00:00:40.540
Wakareta hazu sa

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:43.790
Jigoku wo mireba

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:47.330
Kokoro ga kawaku

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:52.750
Tatakai wa akita no sa

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:57.540
Sadame to areba

00:00:57.710 --> 00:01:00.790
Kokoro wo kimeru

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:05.960
Sottoshite oite kure

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:07.750
Ashita ni

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:15.250
Aa tsunagaru kyou gurai

00:02:14.920 --> 00:02:16.500
Looks like it's begun.

00:02:16.500 --> 00:02:17.500
Yes, sir.

00:02:18.670 --> 00:02:19.630
Where is it?

00:02:19.630 --> 00:02:21.040
Sector 95-D.

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:22.750
Bombed-out zone. Nothing there but rubble.

00:02:23.290 --> 00:02:26.500
Picked an appropriate place to sleep,
didn't you, Chirico?

00:02:26.500 --> 00:02:30.000
Looks like the police are serious about
finishing him off this time.

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:32.330
We have to call the army in at once!

00:02:32.830 --> 00:02:37.130
Don't panic. Our primary objective
is the recovery of the Prototype.

00:02:37.130 --> 00:02:40.790
It isn't too late to wait and see how this battle
between Chirico and the police turns out.

00:02:41.580 --> 00:02:44.080
We'll sit back and wait to see what happens.

00:02:44.130 --> 00:02:49.130
Red Shoulder

00:03:35.670 --> 00:03:36.880
Shut up.

00:03:38.960 --> 00:03:41.380
What's the problem? Be quiet.

00:03:41.880 --> 00:03:44.040
Hey! Don't you hear that?

00:03:44.040 --> 00:03:46.330
Shut up, out there!

00:03:48.290 --> 00:03:51.330
Who's movin' scrap metal around
this early in the morning?

00:03:52.290 --> 00:03:53.880
What's that smell?

00:03:56.330 --> 00:03:57.420
Let's go!

00:04:06.420 --> 00:04:07.500
What the hell?

00:04:13.420 --> 00:04:15.580
What is it? What's going on-

00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:20.670
At this rate, I give us ten minutes
till the fire gets here.

00:04:21.040 --> 00:04:22.580
What the hell's going on?

00:04:23.080 --> 00:04:24.880
The big sweep has started.

00:04:27.080 --> 00:04:28.420
Big sweep?

00:04:28.420 --> 00:04:31.460
They're cleaning up Uoodo by burning it?

00:04:31.460 --> 00:04:33.290
What are you talking about?

00:04:33.290 --> 00:04:34.880
We're the ones getting swept!

00:04:35.960 --> 00:04:36.710
Get down!

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:38.750
Get down!

00:04:46.380 --> 00:04:48.210
It's dangerous to stay here. We have to escape!

00:04:48.710 --> 00:04:50.330
Easy for you to say!

00:04:50.330 --> 00:04:52.750
They just nuked every door into the hideout!

00:05:01.920 --> 00:05:03.540
Then we'll head upwind!

00:05:03.920 --> 00:05:05.330
Choppers! Move it!

00:05:05.330 --> 00:05:06.380
Right!

00:05:12.380 --> 00:05:14.040
No good! Go back!

00:05:25.250 --> 00:05:27.040
We... we're screwed!

00:05:27.040 --> 00:05:29.920
Every place has been blocked!

00:05:53.040 --> 00:05:55.330
This will finally rid us of Chirico.

00:05:55.330 --> 00:05:58.210
We should have done this sooner.

00:06:02.960 --> 00:06:04.920
We're all gonna die here!

00:06:06.420 --> 00:06:09.040
If we get back into the hideout,
we have a chance, right?

00:06:09.040 --> 00:06:11.130
Sure, if we could get back in.

00:06:11.130 --> 00:06:12.460
But we can't!

00:06:12.460 --> 00:06:14.290
All the doors are blocked!

00:06:27.080 --> 00:06:32.040
At the battle of Gyaoa hundreds of
Armored Troopers were burned to death.

00:06:33.210 --> 00:06:35.630
Only three people survived.

00:06:36.130 --> 00:06:38.710
All of them were Red Shoulders.

00:06:39.750 --> 00:06:43.250
You've heard of them, right?
AT Special Forces. Butchers.

00:06:43.250 --> 00:06:45.630
They'd drink their friends' blood to live.

00:06:45.630 --> 00:06:47.210
Eat the flesh of the dead.

00:06:47.210 --> 00:06:50.500
They're supposed to be soldiers
who've crawled straight out of Hell.

00:06:51.130 --> 00:06:53.290
So why are you telling us this?

00:06:53.290 --> 00:06:56.630
I'm not a Red Shoulder! You saying you are?

00:06:57.130 --> 00:07:00.330
And would you stop that constant screaming?

00:07:00.670 --> 00:07:04.210
Crying won't keep us alive! We're all doomed!

00:07:05.920 --> 00:07:07.540
I don't wanna die!

00:07:14.130 --> 00:07:17.130
We don't have time for crying! Help me dig!

00:07:20.420 --> 00:07:23.750
It's impossible! You can't dig
a way in through all this!

00:07:29.170 --> 00:07:30.630
What are you doing? Ow!

00:07:30.630 --> 00:07:32.330
Take a look at this. Right here.

00:07:34.040 --> 00:07:36.040
There's air flowing!

00:07:36.540 --> 00:07:38.420
I don't think this pile's very deep.

00:07:38.420 --> 00:07:39.710
It's too soon to give up.

00:07:39.710 --> 00:07:41.830
Well, this changes things.

00:07:41.830 --> 00:07:43.500
To hell with dying!

00:08:21.250 --> 00:08:22.630
We did it!

00:08:44.210 --> 00:08:45.790
Whoops, I fell.

00:08:50.580 --> 00:08:51.880
Here it is.

00:08:53.210 --> 00:08:55.170
There's a hole down here?

00:08:55.920 --> 00:08:58.290
Even I haven't gone down there yet.

00:08:58.290 --> 00:09:00.630
I think there're pipes running below this floor.

00:09:00.630 --> 00:09:03.960
If we're lucky, we might be able
to get to the next block.

00:09:03.960 --> 00:09:06.170
All right, I'll try to get down there.

00:09:45.330 --> 00:09:47.380
Explosions. We're not safe here, either.

00:09:47.380 --> 00:09:48.210
Chirico!

00:09:48.210 --> 00:09:49.210
Gimme some rope!

00:09:49.380 --> 00:09:51.290
There's no place to stand. I need some rope!

00:09:51.290 --> 00:09:52.210
Gotcha!

00:09:52.210 --> 00:09:54.130
And a short length of pipe, too!

00:10:17.330 --> 00:10:19.580
All right, come down one at a time.

00:10:19.580 --> 00:10:23.290
Okay, I'll go. I can check out what's up ahead.

00:10:35.630 --> 00:10:37.710
I've never feel comfortable in situations like this.

00:10:37.710 --> 00:10:39.790
You're a pilot and you're scared of heights?

00:10:39.790 --> 00:10:41.960
Excuse me for being scared.

00:10:44.080 --> 00:10:45.500
Coconna, you're next.

00:10:58.380 --> 00:11:00.130
Thanks, Chirico.

00:11:03.080 --> 00:11:04.540
Move it, old man!

00:11:04.540 --> 00:11:05.420
Coming!

00:11:06.750 --> 00:11:08.500
Careful, Coconna.

00:11:11.790 --> 00:11:12.580
Come on.

00:11:14.790 --> 00:11:15.670
Gotcha!

00:11:26.670 --> 00:11:27.460
Chirico!

00:12:28.080 --> 00:12:29.250
Just as I thought.

00:12:29.250 --> 00:12:30.330
You did it!

00:12:30.750 --> 00:12:33.330
They've even got water in here!

00:12:33.330 --> 00:12:35.210
So, what would you like to eat?

00:12:36.460 --> 00:12:37.920
Chirico, come on.

00:12:38.420 --> 00:12:39.880
What looks good?

00:12:39.880 --> 00:12:41.380
What, don't you need any?

00:12:41.920 --> 00:12:43.750
I'll get food in the city.

00:12:44.330 --> 00:12:46.670
Don't tell me you want to go back!

00:12:47.040 --> 00:12:49.080
We haven't settled this.

00:12:49.540 --> 00:12:51.290
You're really serious!

00:12:56.880 --> 00:12:59.960
If they find you, you'll die.

00:12:59.960 --> 00:13:01.960
We have to get out of this city.

00:13:01.960 --> 00:13:04.040
Yeah, and we can't afford to wait!

00:13:07.250 --> 00:13:09.960
Maybe it's time I told you.

00:13:12.380 --> 00:13:16.830
The reason they're after me is because
I saw something incredible during the war.

00:13:17.000 --> 00:13:18.540
Something incredible?

00:13:18.880 --> 00:13:19.920
What was it?

00:13:20.830 --> 00:13:21.670
A woman.

00:13:21.920 --> 00:13:23.040
A woman?

00:13:23.040 --> 00:13:24.880
Not an ordinary woman.

00:13:24.880 --> 00:13:26.040
Then what?

00:13:26.290 --> 00:13:27.790
A military secret.

00:13:28.790 --> 00:13:30.960
She's with the police now.

00:13:30.960 --> 00:13:34.420
I don't want to leave the city
until I know who she is.

00:13:35.000 --> 00:13:37.540
Don't you want to live?

00:13:37.540 --> 00:13:39.130
I don't die so easily.

00:13:39.880 --> 00:13:42.210
If you want to come, I wouldn't mind.

00:13:42.630 --> 00:13:44.790
That's okay. No thanks.

00:13:44.790 --> 00:13:46.080
Me, neither.

00:13:46.080 --> 00:13:48.040
And what about you, Miss Manager?

00:13:50.580 --> 00:13:52.670
It's too dangerous! Chirico...

00:13:53.880 --> 00:13:54.920
Goodbye, then.

00:14:16.210 --> 00:14:17.170
Chirico...

00:14:25.630 --> 00:14:29.750
We haven't actually found any bodies yet,
but the place is burned to the ground.

00:14:29.750 --> 00:14:31.960
Chirico must be dead!

00:14:32.960 --> 00:14:36.540
Well, until you find the bodies,
keep searching for him!

00:14:36.540 --> 00:14:37.460
Sir!

00:14:46.920 --> 00:14:48.380
Where are you going?

00:14:48.380 --> 00:14:49.790
To my room.

00:14:52.670 --> 00:14:53.880
Strange.

00:14:53.880 --> 00:14:55.000
What?

00:14:55.000 --> 00:14:57.250
Her emotional response is too strong.

00:14:57.960 --> 00:14:59.540
Of course.

00:14:59.540 --> 00:15:01.710
Our "Perfect Soldier" is still just a young girl.

00:15:01.710 --> 00:15:03.500
That's not what I mean.

00:15:03.500 --> 00:15:06.960
The Prototype seems to have
special feelings for Chirico.

00:15:06.960 --> 00:15:07.830
What?

00:15:07.830 --> 00:15:09.580
They've met before.

00:15:09.960 --> 00:15:11.670
They must have.

00:15:11.670 --> 00:15:13.920
There's no other explanation.

00:16:21.420 --> 00:16:25.330
In this day and age, you never know
when violence will strike!

00:16:25.330 --> 00:16:29.040
But when it does, we have the gun for you!
The 24-round Atomic Magnum!

00:16:29.040 --> 00:16:31.460
Pure killing power for self-defense!

00:16:31.710 --> 00:16:35.580
Can kill anything up to 50 meters away
within a 30 degree firing arc.

00:16:35.580 --> 00:16:38.040
Pretty boring, with no matches going on.

00:16:38.750 --> 00:16:43.080
Gotta expect this when
the cops start cracking down.

00:16:43.080 --> 00:16:45.750
Yeah, but a month is an awfully long time.

00:16:45.750 --> 00:16:48.460
The ATs in the garage are gonna start to rust!

00:16:48.460 --> 00:16:49.630
Yeah, right.

00:16:50.040 --> 00:16:51.250
I'm going out for a bit.

00:16:51.250 --> 00:16:54.040
Sure. Don't be late for the shift change!

00:16:54.040 --> 00:16:55.420
I gotcha.

00:16:57.420 --> 00:16:58.380
I love it!

00:16:58.380 --> 00:16:59.170
Me, too!

00:16:59.170 --> 00:17:00.080
Give me more!

00:17:00.080 --> 00:17:01.170
Me, too!

00:17:01.170 --> 00:17:03.380
When that summer thirst hits,
only one thing refreshes!

00:17:03.380 --> 00:17:04.630
Meetu Beer!

00:17:04.960 --> 00:17:07.040
What, did you forget something?

00:17:08.920 --> 00:17:10.080
Who are you?

00:17:53.920 --> 00:17:55.290
What's wrong, Coconna?

00:17:55.750 --> 00:17:57.290
I'm not going.

00:17:57.500 --> 00:18:00.000
Now what're you talking about?

00:18:00.830 --> 00:18:04.500
Look, it's just a three day walk
and we're out of their jurisdiction.

00:18:04.500 --> 00:18:07.880
Then we get a car and go wherever we please.

00:18:07.880 --> 00:18:10.000
I'm going back to look for Chirico.

00:18:10.210 --> 00:18:11.580
What, that again?

00:18:11.830 --> 00:18:13.580
I'm worried about him!

00:18:13.580 --> 00:18:16.580
Who cares what happens to a guy like that?

00:18:17.130 --> 00:18:19.880
Thought you said you were
coming with us for your own sake.

00:18:19.880 --> 00:18:21.750
Well, I decided differently!

00:18:28.880 --> 00:18:30.920
For crying out loud. Women!

00:18:31.250 --> 00:18:34.710
Ready to throw her life away
for some guy she loves.

00:18:34.710 --> 00:18:36.040
You can say that again.

00:18:53.920 --> 00:18:55.670
Sorry I'm late!

00:18:55.880 --> 00:18:57.540
What, are you asleep?

00:18:59.170 --> 00:18:59.960
Hey!

00:19:35.830 --> 00:19:38.460
Is this the police? Have I got a tip for you!

00:19:38.460 --> 00:19:40.460
That guy you're looking for, Chirico?

00:19:40.460 --> 00:19:41.790
He's right here! The Battling stadium-

00:19:42.630 --> 00:19:43.750
Ow!

00:19:44.880 --> 00:19:46.080
Why, you...!

00:19:47.500 --> 00:19:48.830
Ow!

00:19:50.920 --> 00:19:52.790
What the... You're just a girl!

00:19:58.290 --> 00:20:00.790
What are you trying to do by yourself?

00:20:00.790 --> 00:20:02.830
Vanilla! Pops!

00:20:02.830 --> 00:20:05.540
The cops know that Chirico's here!

00:20:05.540 --> 00:20:06.670
What?
What?

00:20:06.670 --> 00:20:07.830
Not good.

00:20:16.170 --> 00:20:17.830
Wait, it's us! It's us!

00:20:18.670 --> 00:20:19.830
Why are you...

00:20:21.080 --> 00:20:22.670
You changed your minds?

00:20:22.670 --> 00:20:24.330
Never mind why!

00:20:24.630 --> 00:20:27.250
What in blue blazes is that?

00:20:32.920 --> 00:20:35.170
You look like you're going to start a war.

00:20:35.170 --> 00:20:36.630
You could say that.

00:20:36.630 --> 00:20:39.290
No time to relax! The cops know you're here!

00:20:39.670 --> 00:20:40.750
Really...?

00:20:40.750 --> 00:20:43.710
We have to run! They'll be here soon!

00:20:43.710 --> 00:20:47.040
I can't leave here until this is finished.

00:20:47.040 --> 00:20:51.000
But you've got a missile launcher
and a vulcan cannon mounted!

00:20:51.000 --> 00:20:52.830
You think you can use all those?

00:20:52.830 --> 00:20:55.330
I have to mount the control box on the back.

00:20:55.710 --> 00:20:56.880
And an ammo pack, too.

00:20:56.880 --> 00:21:00.210
Hell, I'll do it! It'll be faster this way!

00:21:02.210 --> 00:21:02.920
Me, too!

00:21:02.920 --> 00:21:03.580
And me!

00:21:10.330 --> 00:21:12.630
Left more! More! More!

00:21:24.710 --> 00:21:26.920
How do you like the color, Chirico?

00:21:26.920 --> 00:21:29.830
You're a Red Shoulder, emmissary from Hell!

00:21:31.960 --> 00:21:33.750
What do you think, Chirico?

00:21:35.000 --> 00:21:37.880
The Red Shoulders use a deeper shade.
The color of blood.

00:21:37.880 --> 00:21:39.960
And it would be on the right shoulder.

00:21:41.750 --> 00:21:44.920
He can see it's all wrong with just one look!

00:21:45.420 --> 00:21:48.130
Chirico, are you... You're a Red Shoulder?

00:21:48.130 --> 00:21:53.170
The official designation is Melkian Strategic
Armored Trooper Special Operations Corps X-1.

00:21:53.170 --> 00:21:55.500
People called us the Blood Sucker Battallion.

00:21:57.040 --> 00:22:00.500
Oh, this is too much!
I knew we could count on you!

00:22:00.500 --> 00:22:03.380
With you, we could take on the devil himself!

00:22:18.670 --> 00:22:20.960
We've spotted Chirico. No resistance yet.

00:22:20.960 --> 00:22:22.750
Looks like he isn't alone in there.

00:22:22.750 --> 00:22:24.630
Never mind! Move in!

00:22:28.040 --> 00:22:29.420
They're here.

00:22:34.000 --> 00:22:37.460
"They could never understand the pain
of being a Red Shoulder."

00:22:38.080 --> 00:22:42.040
Thinking that, I prepared to meet
the advancing enemy.

00:22:42.960 --> 00:22:45.790
Only by fighting could I forget
the horrors I'd seen.

00:22:46.420 --> 00:22:48.540
I fought on only so I wouldn't remember.

00:22:49.000 --> 00:22:50.830
But, someday...

00:22:54.290 --> 00:22:55.710
Next Episode

00:22:56.540 --> 00:23:00.170
The steel warrior runs, leaps, and howls.

00:23:00.170 --> 00:23:02.830
Machine guns roar, missiles fly forth.

00:23:03.000 --> 00:23:05.880
A steel arm forces open the doorway to a mystery.

00:23:06.170 --> 00:23:09.670
As he turns towards the waiting flames,
what is the flickering shadow he sees?

00:23:10.040 --> 00:23:13.580
Now, more reasons behind the
Lido operation are revealed.

00:23:13.580 --> 00:23:16.920
As is the truth behind the mysterious Prototype.

00:23:17.460 --> 00:23:19.380
Next time, "Counterattack"

00:23:19.920 --> 00:23:21.790
Chirico assaults the inner sanctum.

00:23:20.330 --> 00:23:24.290
Counterattack

00:23:20.330 --> 00:23:24.290
Next Time

00:23:42.540 --> 00:23:46.000
Samishii toki mo

00:23:46.000 --> 00:23:49.540
Kanashii toki mo

00:23:49.540 --> 00:23:55.920
Itsumo anata ga me ni ukabu

00:23:56.420 --> 00:23:59.960
Hitori no toki mo

00:23:59.960 --> 00:24:03.380
Aitai toki mo

00:24:03.380 --> 00:24:09.630
Itsumo anata wa mune no naka

00:24:09.630 --> 00:24:13.130
Tooku hanarete itemo

00:24:13.130 --> 00:24:16.540
Tatoe wakarete itemo

00:24:16.710 --> 00:24:23.040
Kono yo no hikari to tomo ni mabushiku

00:24:23.420 --> 00:24:29.380
Ano hi no anata ga...
